WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.480
Raj: Okay, packet loss reaches roughly two percent. That's from the five-minute probe window.

2
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:15.791
Hannah: Are those probes ICMP or application traffic? Diagnostic responses can be rate-limited separately.

3
00:00:15.791 --> 00:00:23.687
Raj: ICMP, plus actual TCP retransmission samples. Jitter rises in the same recorded periods.

4
00:00:23.687 --> 00:00:29.662
Lukas: Does that prove where the loss occurs? We still need both endpoint observations.

5
00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:37.270
Anika: No, the working hypothesis is path degradation. Client timeout bursts align with those periods.

6
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:44.926
Priya: Just to confirm, not a location claim, right? Evidence links timing, not the faulty device.

7
00:00:44.926 --> 00:00:52.581
Hannah: Right, we can't rule that out yet. Congestion and physical errors need separate checks.

8
00:00:52.581 --> 00:00:59.325
Raj: I'll keep an eye on interface counters. They've stayed clean at our local endpoint.

9
00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:05.708
Lukas: Save counters with the same timestamps. Clean local counters don't clear the remote side.

10
00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:12.740
Priya: So, keep the conclusion narrow for now. Next, review what the carrier actually promised.

